do GameState.start_minigame()
[background arg="res://assets/Minigame/Minigame_1.png" fade="1.0" transition="Push Up"]
audio music "res://audio/higheruniversalman-take-me-out-to-the-ball-game-sports-stadium-crowd-music-506221.mp3" [volume="-14.0" loop="true"]
join "Lady MacDeath" center [mirrored="true"]
[wait time="1.5"]
Lizzy: Lady MacDeath, the time loop is happening.
Lizzy: And I have proof!
label Journal Select
do MenuManager.open_journal()
[wait_input]
if {is_success} == true:
	do MinegameTest.update_background("strikes_number")
	if {current_item} == "pocket_shakespeare":
		Lizzy: i found this heavily annotated shakespeare book in the graveyard in one of the loops.
		"Lady MacDeath": I was looking for that.
		Lizzy: I've read some of the notes and you've really torn old Willy S apart.
		"Lady MacDeath": I loath the man.
		"Lady MacDeath": He was quite obtuse when I first met him and then my husband became obsessed and dragged me to every showing.
		"Lady MacDeath": One can only take so many misperformances of Taming of the Shrew and Romeo and Juilet.
		"Lady MacDeath": More like Groaneo and Juilget me out of there.
		"Lady MacDeath": I celebrated when Hamnet died.
		Lizzy: Isn’t it Hamlet?
		"Lady MacDeath": Hamnet was Shakespeares son.
		Lizzy: ...
		Lizzy: That’s dark.
		"Lady MacDeath": I’m an evil vampire. What do you expect?
	
	elif {current_item} == "lm_dagger_vouch":
		Dagger: My Lady, Elizabeth speaks the truth.
		Dagger: We are stuck in a time loop.
		"Lady MacDeath": You are weak when it comes to this werewolf pup.
		Lizzy: I’m not that young...
		"Lady MacDeath": But you are quite honest when it really comes down to it.
		"Lady MacDeath": I've been meaning to talk to you about that, actually.
		"Lady MacDeath": It is beyond irritating.
		Dagger: Of course, my lady. I will work on this flaw of character.
		Lizzy: Are you kidding me?
		Lizzy: You're letting her walk all over you, man!
		Dagger: What would you have me do?
		Dagger: We want to convince her, right?
		Lizzy: Yeah, but,
		Lizzy: Stand up for yourself.
		"Lady MacDeath": Elizabeth Springs is right.
		"Lady MacDeath": Have back bone, Dagger, darling.
		"Lady MacDeath": It's embarrassing.
		"Lady MacDeath": ...
		"Lady MacDeath": Perhaps we are more alike than I've previously assumed, young werewolf.
		Lizzy: You seem pretty cool too, for an evil vampire.
	
	
	elif {current_item} == "d_zombie_plan":
		Lizzy: i know all about your zombie plan!
		"Lady MacDeath": Dagger told you.
		"Lady MacDeath": I knew he was leaking previous information.
		Lizzy: No. You attacked me in a previous loop and then you said something along the lines of
		Lizzy: "Watch as my undead army eats everybody you love muhahahahha~"
		"Lady MacDeath": That does sound like me.
	
	set {strikes_number} += 1.0
	join Item leftmost [animation="Zoom In" length="9.0"]
	leave Item [animation="Slide To Right" length="1.1" wait="true"]
	if {strikes_number} == 1.0:
		[background arg="res://assets/Minigame/Minigame_2.png" fade="0.0" transition="Simple Fade"]
	elif {strikes_number} == 2.0:
		[background arg="res://assets/Minigame/Minigame_3.png" fade="0.0" transition="Simple Fade"]
	elif {strikes_number} == 3.0:
		[background arg="res://assets/Minigame/Minigame_4.png" fade="0.0" transition="Simple Fade"]
	[wait time="1.5"]
else:
	"Lady MacDeath": And this is supposed to mean something to me because....?
	Lizzy: Uh... I was just testing to see if you're paying attention.
	[V.O] I'll have to try something else.
set {is_success} = false
if {strikes_number} < 3.0:
	jump Journal Select
[background fade="2.0" wait="true"]
audio music - [fade="4.0"]
"Lady MacDeath": You've made a compelling argument.
do GameState.end_minigame()
jump ending_6/